  "case_sources": {
    "prices": "Eurostat nrg_pc_205 (electricity, band ID 2,000-19,999 MWh) and nrg_pc_203 (gas, band I3 10,000-99,999 GJ), Portugal, 2026-S1, excluding VAT and other recoverable taxes and levies, EUR/kWh (gas on GCV). Parsed copy: data/sources/eurostat_portugal_prices.csv. Band check: gas fuel ~ 1.2e7 kWh/year = 43,000 GJ (I3); heat pump electricity alone 3.4 GWh/year (ID); site electricity 7.5-11.5 kWh/hl for breweries above 1 Mhl/y (IFC EHS Guidelines for Breweries 2007, Table 3) + heat pumps 3.4-3.9 kWh/hl = 11-15 GWh/year: band ID. ID is also the conservative choice (dearer than IE)",
    "boiler_efficiency": "DEA Technology Data - Industrial Process Heat, sheet 6.1 (2025): 93.9 % net (NCV) annual average, steam boiler with economiser; x 0.90 (NCV/GCV) = 0.845 on the GCV basis of the gas price. Gas prices are on GCV: Regulation (EU) 2016/1952, Annex I, point 4; NCV/GCV = 0.90: IPCC (1996) Reference Manual, Ch. 1, Table 1-4 note a (10 % for natural gas)",
    "operating_hours_per_year": "published: Padullés et al. (2026), Sec. 5.1",
    "discount_rate, horizon_years": "published: Padullés et al. (2026), Sec. 5.2",
    "payback_threshold_years": "research question 1 (5 years)",
    "grid_EF_kg_per_kWh": "APA, Fator de Emissao da Eletricidade - 2025, Table T1: Portugal 2023 = 0.107 t CO2eq/MWh (production-based)",
    "heat_recovery_equipment": "tank 520.8 m3 = 375 m3 x (1.0e6 / 720,000 hl/year), scaled from Padullés et al. (2026), Sec. 5.1",
    "gas_EF_kg_per_kWh": "IPCC 2006 Guidelines Vol. 2 Table 2.2, 56,100 kg CO2/TJ NCV -> 0.182 kg/kWh GCV, direct combustion (same scope as the APA grid factor)",
    "eta_lorenz_sensitivity": "0.45-0.52: Carnot efficiencies implied by DEA HTHP sheets (COP 2.05 at 100 K lift); 0.63: Andersen et al. (2024) polynomial for the HTHP unit (upper envelope, extrapolated: source below 0 °C and isothermal)",
    "co2_price_scenario": "EUA Dec contract 82.40 EUR/t on 5 Oct 2026 (S&P Global Commodity Insights)",
    "chiller_cop": "Sinnott and Towler (2020), Chemical Engineering Design, 6th ed. (Elsevier, ISBN 978-0-08-102599-4), Sec. 6.4.4, Eq. 6.20: real COP about 0.6 x Carnot for a simple cycle. Evaporator at cold utility -1 °C minus 5 K (refrigerated-brine approach 3-5 K, Sec. 12.7.3), condenser at ambient 15 °C + 10 K cooling-water rise + 5 K approach = 30 °C: 0.6 x 267.15/36 = 4.45. Check: CoolProp ammonia cycle (Andersen et al. 2024 assumptions, sink 15->25 °C) gives 4.52. Padullés et al. (2026) give no chiller credit"
